🔌 API Endpoints
Incidents
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/v1/incidents	List all incidents (with filters)
GET	/api/v1/incidents/{id}	Get incident details
POST	/api/v1/incidents	Create new incident
PUT	/api/v1/incidents/{id}	Update incident
DELETE	/api/v1/incidents/{id}	Delete incident
POST	/api/v1/incidents/{id}/resolve	Mark as resolved
Logs
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/logs/upload	Upload log file
GET	/api/v1/logs	Search & filter logs
POST	/api/v1/logs/detect	Trigger incident detection
AI Analysis
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/analysis/root-cause	Get AI root cause
POST	/api/v1/analysis/severity	Classify severity
POST	/api/v1/analysis/summarize	Summarize incident
Remediation
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/remediation/generate	Generate fix steps
POST	/api/v1/remediation/approve	Approve remediation
Workflows
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/workflows/trigger	Trigger workflow
GET	/api/v1/workflows/{id}	Get workflow status
Teams
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/v1/teams	List teams
POST	/api/v1/teams/assign	Assign incident
POST	/api/v1/teams/escalate	Escalate incident
Dashboard
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/v1/dashboard/stats	Get overall stats
GET	/api/v1/dashboard/trends	Get trends
🔄 How It Works
text
1. Log Upload / Ingest
        ↓
2. Log Parser (nginx / app / syslog)
        ↓
3. Incident Detector (rule-based)
        ↓
4. Incident Created in Database
        ↓
5. Gemini API Called
   ├─ Root Cause Analysis
   ├─ Severity Classification
   └─ Remediation Steps
        ↓
6. Workflow Engine Triggered
   ├─ Notify Team
   ├─ Assign Owner
   └─ Escalate if Needed
        ↓
7. Frontend Dashboard Update
   ├─ Live Incident Feed
   ├─ Incident Timeline
   └─ AI Recommendations
🎓 Key Learnings
This project demonstrates:

✅ Clean Architecture — Separated concerns (API / Services / Models / Schemas)

✅ LLM Integration — Real-world AI workflows (not just chatbots)

✅ Prompt Engineering — Structured JSON outputs from Gemini

✅ Full-Stack Development — FastAPI + React end-to-end

✅ Database Design — Time-series incident data modeling

✅ Workflow Automation — Patterns used in real SRE tools

✅ Observability — Log parsing, pattern matching, anomaly detection

